WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.300
Mind your decisions, I'm Presh Talwalkar

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:11.159
The square ABCD has a side length equal to ten. Suppose E is the midpoint of the side AD

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.610
Fold the square from the vertex A

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:20.639
Along the line segment EB in such a way that the point a becomes the point F

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:26.939
The question is what is the distance from the point F to the line segment DC?

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:29.969
I thank Ankit and Amlan for the suggestion

00:00:30.939 --> 00:00:37.319
Pause the video, if you'd like to give this problem a try, and when you're ready keep watching to learn how to solve this problem

00:00:49.989 --> 00:00:54.119
There are many ways to solve this problem and I will present three different methods

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.089
Let's get started by using similar triangles

00:00:58.059 --> 00:01:04.288
First since E is the midpoint of the side AD we have that AE is equal to five

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:11.909
Next consider the right triangle AEB. We can calculate its hypotenuse EB using the Gougu Theorem

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:16.140
EB is equal to the square root of five squared plus 10 squared, which means

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.659
EB is equal to five times the square root of five

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:25.860
Construct AF. Let its intersection with the line EB be the point G

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:33.030
Since E is equidistant from the points A and F and B is equidistant from the points A and F

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.420
EB is the perpendicular bisector of AF

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.690
Consequently, these line segments are perpendicular

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:46.199
From here triangle AGE must be similar to triangle BAE

00:01:46.869 --> 00:01:54.779
These are both right triangles that share an equal angle. Therefore we can equate the ratio of the hypotenuse to the longer side

00:01:55.539 --> 00:01:59.699
This means EA over AG is equal to EB over BA

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:03.869
We substitute in the values and then we solve for AG

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:08.609
We simplify to get AG is equal to 10 divided by the square root of 5

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.660
Now what's the length of GF

00:02:13.209 --> 00:02:19.259
Well AG and GF are equal to each other because EB is the perpendicular bisector of AF

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.949
Therefore GF is equal to 10 divided by the square root of 5

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:28.499
now let's construct FH this creates another right triangle and

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:32.099
It shares an angle with the right triangle AGE

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:36.929
therefore AHF is similar to the right triangle AGE

00:02:37.599 --> 00:02:41.639
But from before AGE is similar to the right triangle BAE

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:43.930
therefore

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.530
AHF is similar to the triangle BAE

00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:50.699
This means we have the following ratios that are equal

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:56.610
From here we substitute in the known values and we can simplify and solve for AH

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.060
We get that AH is exactly equal to 8

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:05.160
Now AD, the entire side of the square is equal to 10

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.860
AH plus HD must be equal to 10 and this means HD is equal to 2

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:16.420
But HD is exactly equal to the distance from F to the line segment, DC

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:22.080
Therefore the distance from F to the line segment DC is equal to 2. And that's our answer

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:25.620
Let's now move to the next method of using coordinate geometry

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:33.570
we will first set up a coordinate system will run the x-axis through the bottom side of the square and we'll run the

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:38.790
Y-axis through the left side of the square we can then describe the coordinates of some of these points

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:45.450
The upper corner of the square will be equal to 10 comma 10 because each side of the square has a length equal to 10

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:50.040
Let's now describe the equation for a line that passes through these two points

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:57.329
notice that the line that passes through these two points will have a slope equal to 1/2 and we already know that the

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:59.530
Y-intercept is equal to 5

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.730
therefore we have the equation 1/2 x + 5

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:08.700
We then want to describe the equation of the line that goes through the point 0 10 and F

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:12.059
Notice that since these two lines are perpendicular

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:17.010
The slope of this line will be the negative reciprocal of the first line

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:23.609
So the slope of this line will be equal to negative 2 and we know it's y-intercept is equal to 10

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:28.739
So this line will have an equation that's equal to -2x + 10

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:32.099
To find the intersection of these two lines

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:39.029
We set the equations equal to each other and we can readily solve that X is equal to 2 and Y is equal to 6

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:45.089
Now this point will exactly be the midpoint between 0 10 and F

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.600
Suppose F has the coordinates of P and Q

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:53.250
We thus have 10 + Q, all over 2 is equal to 6

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:58.410
This means Q is equal to 2 and that's exactly the vertical distance

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:03.299
Therefore the distance from F to the line segment DC is equal to 2

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:06.960
Well now move on to the third method of trigonometry

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:13.799
To get started recall that the hypotenuse EB has a length equal to five times the square root of five

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:18.750
Then triangle AEB is congruent to triangle FEB

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:22.439
This means FB has a side length equal to ten

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:30.809
from here suppose angle ABE is equal to theta that means angle EBF is also equal to theta

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:35.790
Now construct FP that's perpendicular to the side AB

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:38.199
consider this triangle

00:05:38.199 --> 00:05:41.369
The sin of two theta will be equal to FP

00:05:41.889 --> 00:05:43.270
divided by ten

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:47.520
We can then use the sin double angle formula from here

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:53.549
We need to calculate the sin of theta and the cos of theta which we can readily get from the triangle ABE

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:59.699
We calculate the values for sin of theta and cos of theta and substitute those into the formula

00:06:00.039 --> 00:06:04.919
We then simplify and we will solve that FP is equal to eight

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:11.399
Now FP is equal to eight but the entire vertical distance is equal to the side of the square

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:17.729
Consequently the distance from F to the side DC is equal to two, just as before

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:22.410
It's a very interesting problem that you can solve in many different ways

00:06:23.139 --> 00:06:30.538
Thanks for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube. As always, thanks for watching and thanks for your support

